      "id": "journal/the-first-mini",
      "type": "Journal",
      "title": "The first Mini",
      "excerpt": "Found it on eBay on Thursday night, in bed, not really looking. Train up to Barnsley on Friday morning, and drove it home.",
      "body": "![The Mini on the seafront, the evening I got it home](assets/journal/first-mini-seafront.jpg)\n\nFound it on eBay on Thursday night, in bed, not really looking. Train up to\nBarnsley on Friday morning, and drove it home.\n\nI have always wanted a Mini, and always wanted one in orange, so getting\nboth at once still feels like a fluke rather than a purchase.\n\nA thousand cc and under 50bhp, so it took the entire day: averaging about\n45mph, with AA cover arranged from every angle I could think of. I had more\nor less accepted I would be sleeping in it on the hard shoulder of a\nmotorway somewhere. It made it the whole way. I do not think I stopped\ngrinning.\n\nThe second photograph is my dad's first Mini, registered the same year as\nmine: both K reg.\n\n![Dad's first Mini, a K reg, from the Bognor Mini Centre](assets/journal/dads-first-mini.jpg)\n\n![An illustration of a Mini in a workshop, drawn in pen and watercolour](assets/journal/mini-garage-watercolour.jpg)\n\n![The same workshop scene, painted](assets/journal/mini-garage-painting.jpg)",
